  "summaries": {
    "en": "Operator deployment order, CC strategies, material farming routes, and Integrated Strategies rogue-like mechanics for Arknights.",
    "ja": "オペレーター配置順、CCステージ戦略、素材ファーミングルート、統合戦略ローグライクメカニックを解説するアークナイツ攻略ガイド。"
  },
  "category": "strategy",
  "difficulty": "advanced",
  "thumbnail": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1561641580-79f91c35eebc?q=80&w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop",
  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "Deployment order is the primary skill gap in Arknights—placing a Guard before a Medic who hasn't been deployed yet results in the Guard taking damage without healing support for 2–4 seconds, which is often lethal on higher difficulty maps.",
      "Block count determines how many enemies an Operator can hold simultaneously—Defenders block 3, Guards block 1–2, Snipers block 0. Deploy Defenders first on choke points, then support characters behind them, then ranged Operators on elevated tiles.",
      "DP (Deployment Points) management determines how many Operators can be deployed simultaneously—high-cost Operators (Supporters, Specialists) require 12–18 DP; pre-generate DP by deploying low-cost vanguards (Courier, Vigna) first to fund high-cost deployments within the first 60 seconds.",
      "Elite Promotion 2 (E2) is the single largest power jump in Arknights—a single E2 Operator contributes more to mission clears than having 6 un-promoted Operators; prioritise promoting one top-tier Operator to E2 before spreading materials.",
      "The Integrated Strategies (IS) mode introduces permanent progression through non-replaceable relics—prioritise Relic choices that benefit your most-used Operator archetypes, not universally strong relics, for the highest long-term IS benefit."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "デプロイ順序はアークナイツにおける主要なスキルギャップ。まだデプロイされていないメディックの前にガードを配置すると、2〜4秒間ヒーリングサポートなしでガードがダメージを受け、高難度マップではしばしば致命的。",
      "ブロック数はオペレーターが同時に保持できる敵の数を決定する。ディフェンダーは3ブロック、ガードは1〜2ブロック、スナイパーは0ブロック。最初にチョークポイントにディフェンダーをデプロイし、その後ろにサポートキャラ、高架タイルに遠隔オペレーターを配置する。",
      "DP（デプロイポイント）管理はいくつのオペレーターを同時にデプロイできるかを決定する。高コストオペレーター（サポーター、スペシャリスト）は12〜18DPが必要。最初の60秒以内に高コストのデプロイに資金を提供するために、まず低コストの先鋒（クーリエ、ヴィーグナ）をデプロイしてDPを事前生成する。",
      "エリート昇進2（E2）はアークナイツの最大のパワージャンプ。未昇進の6体のオペレーターを持つより、E2の1体のトップティアオペレーターの方がミッションクリアに貢献する。素材を広げる前にトップティアオペレーター1体をE2に昇進させることを優先する。",
      "統合戦略（IS）モードは交換不可のレリックによる永続的な進行を導入する。普遍的に強いレリックではなく、最もよく使うオペレーターアーキタイプに利益をもたらすレリックの選択を優先して、最高の長期的なIS利益を得る。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Starter Operator Roster Priority",
        "body": "The starter roster (Amiya, Melantha, Noir Corne, Cardigan, Spot, Adnachiel) covers the essential archetypes: Caster, Guard, Defender, Medic, Sniper. Promote Amiya to Elite 1 first (free promotion at story completion) as she is the highest-damage early Caster and handles the most story chapter bosses. Melantha provides the best early Guard with high block and attack. Fill the remaining slots with your highest-rarity recruited Operators, prioritising 5-star recruitable Operators (Vigna for Vanguard, Myrrh for Medic) before seeking 6-star gacha pulls."
      },
      {
        "title": "Sanity and Material Management",
        "body": "Sanity (AP equivalent) regenerates at 1 per 6 minutes—spend Sanity on the highest material-efficiency farming node for your current E2 promotion target rather than on story stages. The 1-7 stage (a permanent node) is the most efficient long-term LMD (in-game gold) farming node. During Material events, shift all Sanity to event stages for the event duration, then return to permanent farming afterward. Never let Sanity cap (200) without spending it."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Operator Specialisation and Mastery",
        "body": "Skill Mastery upgrades (S1M1 through S3M3) are the most impactful single-Operator power investments. Each Mastery level costs significant materials but provides disproportionate power gains—Skill 3 Mastery 3 on a top-tier DPS Operator (SilverAsh, Surtr, W) provides higher effective DPS than having two equivalent un-mastered Operators. Prioritise S3M3 on your primary damage Operator before investing Masteries on utility Operators."
      },
      {
        "title": "CC (Contingency Contract) Performance",
        "body": "Contingency Contract events add difficulty modifiers in exchange for CC tokens (used to exchange for premium Operators). The minimum CC performance for top rewards requires stacking the highest-penalty modifiers that your roster can handle. Start with Risk 8 clears on the permanent map and increase by 2–4 risk levels per event. Key modifier categories to avoid until E2 roster depth: high deployment limit reductions (below 8 deployments is challenging for most rosters) and GLOBAL attack buff on enemies."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Integrated Strategies and High Risk Runs",
        "body": "Integrated Strategies Risk 18+ requires a curated starting Operator selection and specific relic combinations. The most consistent high-risk IS strategy: start with a Vanguard + Defender core, select the Relic path that provides the Fortification passive (reduces damage taken by all Operators by 15%), and build the mid-run Operator selection around the first-encountered 6-star. At Risk 18, most IS stages require surgical deployment of 2–3 Operators while keeping others in reserve as wave-clear rotations."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Deploying all Operators at once in the opening—deploying all 12 Operators within the first 30 seconds leaves no reserve for retreating and repositioning when enemy waves change direction.",
      "Prioritising 6-star collection over E2 promotions—a single E2-promoted 5-star (e.g., Ptilopsis for Medic) outperforms a 6-star at E1 level in nearly all content; promote before diversifying.",
      "Ignoring Operator Trust building—Trust increases at 0.5% per combat participation; reaching 100% Trust provides unique Trust bonus stats and bonus backstory. High-Trust Operators have a tangible stat advantage in long-term play.",
      "Not reading enemy description before a map—Arknights enemies have specific abilities (Invisible status, Aerial movement, Counter ability) visible in the enemy codex; ignoring these descriptions leads to incorrect Operator selection.",
      "Spending Orundum (premium gacha currency) on non-limited banners—limited banners appear every 4–6 weeks; Orundum saved for limited banners provides higher value per pull than standard banners with permanently available Operators."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "序盤に全てのオペレーターを一度にデプロイする。最初の30秒以内に全12体のオペレーターをデプロイすると、敵の波が方向を変えた時に撤退して再配置する予備がなくなる。",
      "E2昇進よりも6星収集を優先する。E2に昇進した5星（例：メディックのプティロプシス）は、ほぼ全てのコンテンツでE1レベルの6星を上回る。多様化する前に昇進させる。",
      "オペレーターの信頼構築を無視する。信頼は戦闘参加ごとに0.5%増加する。信頼100%達成でユニークな信頼ボーナスステータスとボーナスバックストーリーが得られる。高信頼オペレーターは長期プレイで具体的なステータス優位性を持つ。",
      "マップ前に敵の説明を読まない。アークナイツの敵は敵コデックスで確認できる特定の能力（不可視ステータス、空中移動、カウンター能力）を持つ。これらの説明を無視すると誤ったオペレーター選択につながる。",
      "非限定バナーにオルンダム（プレミアムガチャ通貨）を使う。限定バナーは4〜6週間ごとに登場する。限定バナーのために節約されたオルンダムは、永続的に利用可能なオペレーターを持つ標準バナーよりプル当たりの高い価値を提供する。"
    ]
  },
